<title>LEBANON: Fog diverts three aircraft from Beirut.</title>
<headline>Fog diverts three aircraft from Beirut.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fog at Beirut airport on Monday morning prevented planes from taking off and caused the diversion of three incoming flights to Larnaka airport in Cyprus, officials at the airport said.</p>
<p>A flight of Middle East Airlines, the Lebanese national carrier, arriving from Saudi Arabia, a Jordanian Alia airlines plane from Amman and a private aircraft arriving from Bucharest were diverted, they said.</p>
<p>The airport was reopened at 11 a.m. (0800 GMT), officials added.</p>
